---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/site";
import { localizePath , pick } from "../../i18n/utils";

const lang = (Astro.currentLocale ?? "en") as "en" | "zh";

const slug = "how-to-ssh-from-iphone";

const C = pick({
  en: {
    heading: "How to SSH into a server from your iPhone",
    intro:
      "Add a server, pick an authentication method, and open your first secure shell session on iOS — then drive it with the on-screen keyboard toolbar.",
    meta: "Guide",
    title: "How to SSH from iPhone — VVTerm",
    description:
      "Install VVTerm, add a server, choose password or SSH key auth, connect, and use the keyboard toolbar to SSH into any server from your iPhone.",
    schemaDescription:
      "Step-by-step guide to opening your first SSH session from an iPhone with VVTerm: install, add a server, choose an auth method, connect, and use the keyboard toolbar.",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    VVTerm turns your iPhone into a full SSH client. You can reach any server that accepts SSH —
    a Linux box, a Mac, a Raspberry Pi, a cloud VM — and work in a real GPU-rendered terminal.
    This guide walks through the first connection end to end.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you start</h2>
  <p>
    You need an iPhone running <strong>iOS 16 or later</strong> and a server you can reach over the
    network. Have three things ready: the server's <strong>hostname or IP address</strong>, the <strong>port</strong> (SSH uses <code>22</code> by default), and your <strong>username</strong>.
    If you authenticate with a key instead of a password, have the private key available too.
  </p>

  <h2>Install VVTerm</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the App Store on your iPhone and install VVTerm.</li>
    <li>Launch the app and finish the short welcome flow.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The free tier includes <strong>one server</strong>, which is all you need to follow this guide.
    Pro removes the limits when you want more servers, workspaces, and connection tabs.
  </p>

  <h2>Add your server</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Tap <strong>Add Server</strong> to open the new-server form.</li>
    <li>Give the server a <strong>name</strong> so it's easy to recognize later.</li>
    <li>Enter the <strong>host</strong> — a hostname like <code>example.com</code> or an IP like <code>192.168.1.20</code>.</li>
    <li>Set the <strong>port</strong>. Leave it at <code>22</code> unless your server listens elsewhere.</li>
    <li>Enter the <strong>username</strong> you log in with, for example <code>root</code> or <code>ubuntu</code>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Choose an authentication method</h2>
  <p>VVTerm supports three ways to authenticate, and your credentials are stored in the Apple Keychain — never in synced metadata.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Password</strong> — enter the account password. Simple, and a good way to test that the host and username are correct.</li>
    <li><strong>SSH key</strong> — use a private key for passwordless, more secure login. Paste or import the key, and make sure the matching public key is in the server's <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>SSH key + passphrase</strong> — the same as above, but the private key is itself encrypted with a passphrase for an extra layer of protection.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you don't have a key yet, VVTerm can generate one for you. Add the generated public key to the
    server's <code>authorized_keys</code> file, then select that key as the server's auth method.
  </p>

  <h2>Connect</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Save the server. It appears in your server list.</li>
    <li>Tap the server to open a connection.</li>
    <li>The first time you connect, VVTerm shows the host's key fingerprint so you can verify it before trusting the host.</li>
    <li>Once accepted, the terminal opens and you land at the shell prompt.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Use the keyboard toolbar</h2>
  <p>
    The iOS software keyboard is missing keys that terminals rely on, so VVTerm adds an accessory
    toolbar directly above it. From there you get:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Esc</strong> — essential for vim, less, and most TUI apps.</li>
    <li><strong>Tab</strong> — shell and path completion.</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl</strong> — tap it, then a letter, to send control sequences like <code>Ctrl-C</code> or <code>Ctrl-Z</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Arrow keys</strong> — move the cursor and walk through command history.</li>
    <li><strong>Function keys</strong> — F1 through F12 for apps that map them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can customize the toolbar with your own command snippets, so frequently used commands are one
    tap away.
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <p>
    Your session can survive network drops if you keep it alive with tmux, and you can reach servers
    that aren't directly exposed using <a href="/guides/set-up-mosh-on-ios">Mosh</a>, <a href="/guides/tailscale-ssh-setup">Tailscale SSH</a>, or <a href="/guides/cloudflare-tunnel-ssh-setup">Cloudflare Tunnel SSH</a>. When you need to move files,
    see <a href="/guides/sftp-file-transfer-on-ios">SFTP file transfer on iOS</a>.
  </p>
`,
  },
  zh: {
    heading: "如何从 iPhone SSH 连接服务器",
    intro:
      "添加服务器、选择认证方式，并在 iOS 上开启你的第一个安全 shell 会话 —— 然后用屏幕键盘工具栏来操作它。",
    meta: "指南",
    title: "如何从 iPhone 进行 SSH — VVTerm",
    description:
      "安装 VVTerm、添加服务器、选择密码或 SSH 密钥认证、连接，并使用键盘工具栏从 iPhone SSH 连接任何服务器。",
    schemaDescription:
      "使用 VVTerm 从 iPhone 开启第一个 SSH 会话的分步指南：安装、添加服务器、选择认证方式、连接并使用键盘工具栏。",
    bodyHtml: `
  <p>
    VVTerm 把你的 iPhone 变成一个完整的 SSH 客户端。你可以连接任何接受 SSH 的服务器 ——
    Linux 主机、Mac、树莓派、云端虚拟机 —— 并在真正的 GPU 渲染终端中工作。
    本指南会完整带你走完第一次连接的全过程。
  </p>

  <h2>开始之前</h2>
  <p>
    你需要一台运行 <strong>iOS 16 或更高版本</strong>的 iPhone，以及一台可通过网络访问的服务器。
    准备好三样东西：服务器的<strong>主机名或 IP 地址</strong>、<strong>端口</strong>（SSH 默认使用 <code>22</code>），以及你的<strong>用户名</strong>。
    如果你用密钥而非密码进行认证，还要准备好私钥。
  </p>

  <h2>安装 VVTerm</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>在 iPhone 上打开 App Store 并安装 VVTerm。</li>
    <li>启动应用，完成简短的欢迎流程。</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    免费版包含<strong>一台服务器</strong>，足以完成本指南。
    当你需要更多服务器、工作区和连接标签页时，Pro 会解除这些限制。
  </p>

  <h2>添加你的服务器</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>点按 <strong>Add Server</strong> 打开新建服务器表单。</li>
    <li>给服务器起一个<strong>名称</strong>，方便日后辨认。</li>
    <li>输入<strong>主机</strong> —— 像 <code>example.com</code> 这样的主机名，或像 <code>192.168.1.20</code> 这样的 IP。</li>
    <li>设置<strong>端口</strong>。除非你的服务器监听其他端口，否则保持 <code>22</code>。</li>
    <li>输入你登录用的<strong>用户名</strong>，例如 <code>root</code> 或 <code>ubuntu</code>。</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>选择认证方式</h2>
  <p>VVTerm 支持三种认证方式，你的凭据保存在 Apple Keychain 中 —— 绝不会存于同步的元数据里。</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>密码</strong> —— 输入账户密码。简单直接，也是验证主机和用户名是否正确的好方法。</li>
    <li><strong>SSH 密钥</strong> —— 使用私钥实现免密码、更安全的登录。粘贴或导入密钥，并确保对应的公钥已加入服务器的 <code>~/.ssh/authorized_keys</code>。</li>
    <li><strong>SSH 密钥 + 口令</strong> —— 与上面相同，但私钥本身用口令加密，多加一层保护。</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    如果你还没有密钥，VVTerm 可以为你生成一个。把生成的公钥加入服务器的 <code>authorized_keys</code> 文件，
    然后将该密钥选为服务器的认证方式。
  </p>

  <h2>连接</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>保存服务器，它会出现在你的服务器列表中。</li>
    <li>点按服务器打开连接。</li>
    <li>首次连接时，VVTerm 会显示主机的密钥指纹，便于你在信任该主机前进行核对。</li>
    <li>确认后终端打开，你会进入 shell 提示符。</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>使用键盘工具栏</h2>
  <p>
    iOS 软件键盘缺少终端依赖的一些按键，因此 VVTerm 在其正上方加入了一个辅助工具栏。从那里你可以获得：
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Esc</strong> —— 对 vim、less 和大多数 TUI 应用至关重要。</li>
    <li><strong>Tab</strong> —— shell 和路径补全。</li>
    <li><strong>Ctrl</strong> —— 点按它，再按一个字母，即可发送 <code>Ctrl-C</code> 或 <code>Ctrl-Z</code> 等控制序列。</li>
    <li><strong>方向键</strong> —— 移动光标并浏览命令历史。</li>
    <li><strong>功能键</strong> —— F1 到 F12，供映射了它们的应用使用。</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    你可以用自己的命令片段自定义工具栏，让常用命令一键即达。
  </p>

  <h2>后续步骤</h2>
  <p>
    如果用 tmux 保持会话，你的会话就能在网络中断后存活；你还可以通过 <a href="/zh/guides/set-up-mosh-on-ios">Mosh</a>、<a href="/zh/guides/tailscale-ssh-setup">Tailscale SSH</a> 或 <a href="/zh/guides/cloudflare-tunnel-ssh-setup">Cloudflare Tunnel SSH</a> 连接那些没有直接暴露的服务器。需要传输文件时，
    请参阅 <a href="/zh/guides/sftp-file-transfer-on-ios">在 iOS 上通过 SFTP 传输文件</a>。
  </p>
`,
  },
}, lang);

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  name: C.heading,
  description: C.schemaDescription,
  url: `${SITE.siteUrl}${localizePath(`/guides/${slug}`, lang)}`,
};
---

<DocsLayout
  kind="guides"
  activeSlug={slug}
  heading={C.heading}
  intro={C.intro}
  meta={C.meta}
  title={C.title}
  description={C.description}
  canonicalPath={`/guides/${slug}`}
  structuredData={[articleSchema]}
>
  <Fragment set:html={C.bodyHtml} />
</DocsLayout>
